# Task: peer-review fixes, round 1 (splitwise-pp-cli, Go, hand-authored files only)

Working directory = a generated Go CLI (module `splitwise-pp-cli`). Edit ONLY hand-authored files under `internal/cli/`
(files WITHOUT the `// Generated by CLI Printing Press … DO NOT EDIT` header). Never edit generated files such as
`helpers.go`, `root.go`, `promoted_*.go`. Never run the CLI against `~/.local/share/splitwise-pp-cli/data.db`; use
`--db /tmp/<something>.db` or the test helper `seedSyntheticStore` (internal/cli/split_test.go:21). Do not run `sync`,
`--record`, or `--send`.

## Background (verified facts)
4.31.7's generated `printCSV`/`printPlain` (helpers.go `tabularObjectRows`) flatten ANY non-array object into ONE row
whose cells are Go-formatted (`[map[currency:USD net:4]]`). The hand wrapper `(*rootFlags).emitStructured`
(internal/cli/splitwise_output.go) already guards its callers: single-array envelopes unwrap to a table, anything
else prints the JSON document. But many hand commands still call `flags.printJSON(cmd, v)` directly and therefore emit
garbage under `--csv`/`--plain` — e.g. `net --csv` on an empty store prints `by_currency,plan,savings,you_id` /
`[],[],[],0`. Also `emitStructured`'s csv/plain branches ignore `--select`/`--compact` (only the JSON branch reaches
`filterFields`), and three not-found paths print `Error:` on stderr with empty stdout under `--json` while `settle-up`
emits a JSON error envelope via `novelErr`.

## Edits
1. **splitwise_output.go — `emitStructured`:**
   a. After `json.Marshal(v)` and before any branch, apply the generated helpers when the flags are set:
      `if f.selectFields != "" { raw = filterFields(raw, f.selectFields) }` and
      `if f.compact { raw = compactFields(raw) }` (check the exact field names on `rootFlags` in root.go — grep
      `selectFields` / `compact`). The JSON branch (`f.printJSON`) must NOT double-apply them: pass the original `v`
      there as today (printJSONFiltered applies select/compact itself) — i.e. only the csv/plain branches and their
      JSON fallbacks use the filtered `raw`.
   b. csv fallback and plain fallback both print the (filtered) JSON document, one line/pretty as today.
2. **Route every hand command through the wrapper.** In these hand files replace `flags.printJSON(cmd, X)` with
   `flags.emitStructured(cmd, X)`: activity.go, audit.go, net.go, normalize.go, report.go (2 sites), fairness.go,
   forecast.go, split.go (3 sites), resolve.go (2), reconcile.go (3), fairness_nudge.go (2). In brief.go replace the
   three `printJSONFiltered(cmd.OutOrStdout(), X, flags)` calls with `flags.emitStructured(cmd, X)`. Do not touch
   `splitwise_output.go`'s own `f.printJSON` delegation. Behaviour under `--json`/`--agent` must be byte-identical
   (emitStructured delegates to printJSON for those modes) — verify with `go test`.
3. **JSON error envelope for the three bare not-found returns** — wrap exactly like settle_up.go:84 does:
   ledger.go:93 `return novelErr(cmd, flags, notFoundErr(...))`, split.go:73 same, fairness_nudge.go:79 same.
   `novelErr` is in splitwise_data.go:20 (human mode returns the error unchanged; machine modes print
   `{"error":…,"code":3}` to stdout and silence cobra). Exit code stays 3.
4. **Tests (new, all on synthetic stores):**
   a. `TestHandCommandsCSVNeverFlattenObjects` — table over every hand command that has a store read path
      (activity --since 30d, audit --since 90d, balances, brief, debts, fairness, forecast, ledger "<group>", net,
      normalize --rate EUR=1.1, recurring, report --group "<group>", resolve <name>, spend, settle-up "<group>") on a
      `seedSyntheticStore` fixture (extend the fixture if a command needs groups/friends/expenses; keep names
      synthetic), for both `--csv` and `--plain`: assert stdout is EITHER a valid JSON document OR parses with
      `encoding/csv` (tab-split for --plain) with a header row, AND no cell/line contains `map[` or `[map[`. Skip
      commands that legitimately print nothing on an empty result (`resolve` with no match) by asserting empty
      stdout is OK only when exit code is 0/3 and stderr explains. This test MUST fail on the pre-fix code for
      net/activity/audit/normalize/report (confirm by temporarily reverting edit 2 if you want; then re-apply).
   b. `TestEmitStructured_CSVHonoursSelect` and `TestEmitStructured_PlainMultiArrayFallsBackToJSON` in
      emit_structured_test.go (mirror the existing tests; for select, a two-array envelope + `--select` of one
      array field must yield only that field).
   c. Extend `TestNovelTypedExitCodes` (exit_codes_test.go): add `fairness nudge Missing --json` → 3 using
      `nudgeFixture(t,false)` (see fairness_nudge_test.go) so the NOT-FOUND branch (not the empty-store branch) runs;
      and for the four fixture commands under `--json` assert stdout unmarshals to `{"code":3,"error":<non-empty>}`
      and stderr contains no `Error:` line.
   d. `TestHappyArgsAnnotationsWellFormed` — for fairness nudge, ledger, settle-up, split: split
      `Annotations["pp:happy-args"]` on `;`; each token matches `^<[a-z-]+>=\S` or `^--[a-z-]+(=.+)?$`; every
      `--flag` exists via `cmd.Flags().Lookup`; the `<label>` text appears in `cmd.Use`; `pp:typed-exit-codes`
      contains `3`.
5. **Fixture hygiene:** in splitwise_balances_bygroup_test.go rename the group "Barcelona" to "Example Trip"
   everywhere it appears (it coincides with a real group name).

## Verify before finishing
`go build ./... && go vet ./... && go test -count=1 ./internal/cli/` green; then build the binary
(`go build -o ./splitwise-pp-cli ./cmd/splitwise-pp-cli`) and show: `./splitwise-pp-cli net --csv --db /tmp/x.db`
