 succeeded in 0ms:
Splitwise CLI — Every Splitwise feature, plus an offline SQLite ledger that powers balance, debt-aging, spend analytics, fairness, and full-text search no other Splitwise tool has.

Highlights (not in the official API docs):
  • balances   See everything you owe and are owed across every friend and group in one net-position view.
  • settle-up   Compute the minimum set of transfers that zeroes out balances in a group, then optionally record the payments.
  • audit   Catch duplicate settlement rows and abnormal expense amounts before you trust a settle-up plan.
  • debts   List who owes you (and whom you owe) sorted by how long the balance has gone unsettled.
  • spend   Total shared spend broken down by category, group, or month from your synced history.
  • fairness   See who's carrying more than their share of cost, and how likely a stale balance is to actually get paid.
  • net   Collapse a person's balance across every group and non-group expense into the minimum set of real-world transfers.
  • report   Turn synced trip or period spend into a shareable summary plus per-person and per-category export.
  • ledger   Every expense in a group, in date order, with a cumulative running balance per member.
  • split   Build and preview the exact expense split (equal, exact, percentage, or shares) before recording it.
  • recurring   Surface repeating charges (rent, utilities, subscriptions) from your synced history and flag a cycle missing an expected entry.
  • fairness nudge   Post a payment reminder as a comment on the actual open expense thread, previewed before it sends.
  • balances   See one row per group per currency for every non-zero balance, without the noise of settled groups.
  • brief   Get one compact digest of net position, the stalest debts, and what changed since last sync in a single call.
  • reconcile   Verify the local store actually matches Splitwise before you trust a settle-up or report (calls the live Splitwise API; needs SPLITWISE_API_KEY and network).
  …and 3 more — see README.md for the full list

Agent mode: add --agent to any command for JSON output + non-interactive mode.
Health check: run 'splitwise-pp-cli doctor' to verify auth and connectivity.
See README.md or the bundled SKILL.md for recipes.

Usage:
  splitwise-pp-cli [command]

Available Commands:
  activity               Show recent notifications and expenses changed within a time window
  add-user-to-group      **Note**: 200 OK does not indicate a successful response. You must check the `success` value of the response.
  agent-context          Emit structured JSON describing this CLI for agents
  api                    Browse all API endpoints by interface name
  audit                  Audit synced expenses for likely duplicates and per-category cost outliers
  auth                   Manage authentication for Splitwise
  balances               Show your net balance per friend from the synced store, or per currency (--by-currency) or per group (--by-group)
  brief                  One compact digest: net position, stalest debts, and recent changes.
  completion             Generate the autocompletion script for the specified shell
  create-comment         Create a comment
  create-expense         Creates an expense. You may either split an expense equally (only with `group_id` provided), or supply a list of shares.
  create-friend          Adds a friend. If the other user does not exist, you must supply `user_first_name`.
  create-friends         Add multiple friends at once.
  create-group           Creates a new group. Adds the current user to the group by default.
  debts                  List who owes whom from synced balances, sorted by days since the last settled point (--aged)
  delete-comment         Deletes a comment. Returns the deleted comment.
  delete-expense         **Note**: 200 OK does not indicate a successful response. The operation was successful only if `success` is true.
  delete-friend          Given a friend ID, break off the friendship between the current user and the specified user.
  delete-group           Delete an existing group. Destroys all associated records (expenses, etc.)
  doctor                 Check CLI health
  export                 Export data to JSONL or JSON for backup, migration, or analysis
  fairness               Score who carries the group, who's a collection risk, and who to chase or write off
  feedback               Record feedback about this CLI (local by default; upstream opt-in)
  forecast               Project upcoming shared obligations from recurring spending patterns
  get-categories         Returns a list of all categories Splitwise allows for expenses.
  get-comments           Get expense comments
  get-currencies         Returns a list of all currencies allowed by the system.
  get-current-user       Get information about the current user
  get-expense            Get expense information
  get-expenses           List the current user's expenses
  get-friend             Get details about a friend
  get-friends            **Note**: `group` objects only include group balances with that friend.
  get-group              Get information about a group
  get-groups             **Note**: Expenses that are not associated with a group are listed in a group with ID 0.
  get-notifications      Return a list of recent activity on the users account with the most recent items first.
  get-user               Get information about another user
  help                   Help about any command
  import                 Import data from JSONL file via API create/upsert calls
  learnings              Inspect or forget the local search_learnings table
  ledger                 Replay a group's expenses in date order with a running balance per member, or one friend across all groups (--friend)
  net                    Net balances across all groups into the fewest direct transfers
  normalize              Normalize multi-currency net and spend into one base currency using user-supplied FX rates
  playbook               Inspect or amend stored CLI playbooks
  profile                Named sets of flags saved for reuse
  recall                 Check prior learnings for a query before running discovery (LLM-fired, pre-discovery)
  reconcile              Verify the local expense mirror against the live API: report missing, stale, and remotely-deleted expenses.
  recurring              Surface repeating charges (rent, utilities, subscriptions) from synced history
  remove-user-from-group Remove a user from a group. Does not succeed if the user has a non-zero balance.
  report                 Export an offline trip/period spend report (md/csv/json; PDF out of scope in v1)
  resolve                Resolve a friend, group, or category name to its Splitwise id from the local store (no network)
  search                 Search locally synced data
  settle-up              Compute a settle-up transfer plan and optionally record payment expenses
  spend                  Show your spend (your share of each expense) grouped by category, group, or month
  split                  Build and preview an expense split, then optionally record it
  sync                   Sync API data to local SQLite for offline search and analysis
  tail                   Stream live changes by polling the API at regular intervals
  teach                  Record a query -> resource mapping for future recall (LLM-fired, silent)
  teach-lookup           Install a manual entity-lookup row (kind, canonical, value)
  teach-pattern          Install a manual generalization pattern (query_template, resource_template, entity_kind)
  teach-playbook         Record a CLI playbook + free-text notes for a query family
  undelete-expense       **Note**: 200 OK does not indicate a successful response. The operation was successful only if `success` is true.
  undelete-group         Restores a deleted group. **Note**: 200 OK does not indicate a successful response.
  update-expense         Updates an expense.
  update-user            Update a user
  version                Print version
  which                  Find the command that implements a capability
  workflow               Compound workflows that combine multiple API operations

Flags:
      --agent                   Set agent-friendly output defaults (--json --compact --no-input --no-color)
      --allow-partial-failure   Downgrade response-body partial-failure (e.g. partialFailureError) to a warning instead of a non-zero exit
      --audit-dir string        Aggregate the receipt and index under this audit directory
      --client-profile string   Select the tenant-gated client profile (env: PRINTING_PRESS_CLIENT_PROFILE)
      --compact                 Return only key fields (id, name, status, timestamps) for minimal token usage
      --config string           Config file path
      --csv                     Output as CSV (table and array responses)
      --data-source string      Data source for read commands: auto (live with local fallback), live (API only), local (synced data only) (default "auto")
      --deliver string          Route output to a sink: stdout (default), file:<path>, webhook:<url>
      --dry-run                 Show request without sending
  -h, --help                    help for splitwise-pp-cli
      --home string             Root directory for config, data, state, and cache files
      --human-friendly          Enable colored output and rich formatting
      --idempotent              Treat already-existing create results as a successful no-op
      --json                    Output as JSON
      --max-age duration        Maximum acceptable age of local-store data before a stderr hint suggests sync; 0 disables (default 30m0s)
      --no-cache                Bypass response cache
      --no-color                Disable colored output
      --no-input                Disable all interactive prompts (for CI/agents)
      --no-learn                Disable the teach/recall learning loop for this invocation
      --plain                   Output as plain tab-separated text
      --profile string          Apply values from a saved run profile; this does not select a client (see 'splitwise-pp-cli profile list')
      --quiet                   Bare output, one value per line
      --rate-limit float        Max requests per second (0 to disable; default auto — pace to server rate-limit headers) (default auto)
      --receipt                 Write an atomic private run receipt
      --receipt-file string     Override the run receipt destination
      --select string           Comma-separated fields to include in output
      --timeout duration        Request timeout (default 1m0s)
  -v, --version                 version for splitwise-pp-cli
      --yes                     Skip confirmation prompts (explicit confirmation for scripts)

Use "splitwise-pp-cli [command] --help" for more information about a command.
